                            EBS
                    Elastic Block Storage

**AWS provides two types of storage for instance:
1. Instant store
2. EBS:
--> EBS is a block level storage service it provides persistent storage to ec2 instance.

                       **Snapshot**

--> EBS snapshots are point in time image/copy of your EBS volume.
--> Per account upto 5000 EBS volume can be created.
--> Per acount upto 10000 EBS snapshots can be created.
--> Volumes are AZ specific, snapshots are region specific.
--> EBS snapshot is an incremental data backup
--> the first backup of a volume backsup all the data.
--> Every next  backup copies only a block od data that has changed since last snapshot
